							<h4>Guide</h4>
							<p>The anime is ordered by default (but you can always check the <a href="/">home page</a> if you want).</p>
							<p>There are a lot of options for subs, so read carefully to understand which one suits your needs:</p>
							<ul>
								<li><b>English:</b> MTBB is the only valid choice if you want consistency and very good translation. In this case, you have two options, "eng" and "enm". Select "enm" if you want honorifics (-kun, -san, -sama), or "eng" if you don't. I really recommend using the honorifics as they are crucial for some jokes and context.</li>
								<li><b>Spanish:</b> Ñyuum subs are Castilian Spanish, and they don't include typesettings (translation of visual elements, like signs). All the other Spanish tracks are Latin American Spanish.</li>
								<li><b>Portuguese (Brazil):</b> Anipakku & Yami subs are the best choice when it's available, otherwise use the ones you see fit.</li>
							</ul>
